course: dictionary
lesson: 12247
title: Constipated
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Constipated is a word about your body. If you cannot empty your bowels easily, you are constipated. Your poo may be hard and dry, or it may not come for days. «After the long journey, Sam felt constipated and had a sore tummy.» Sam's tummy hurts and he cannot go to the toilet easily, so constipated must mean unable to empty your bowels easily.
explain: Doctors and nurses talk about constipation in health lessons, because food and drink can help. «Eating apples, beans and wholegrain bread can help stop you getting constipated.» These foods are full of fibre, which helps your poo move along. Water and moving about also help.
explain: You can use constipated in everyday talk. You can say «I feel constipated» or «I get constipated when I eat too many sweets and not enough fruit.» If you feel constipated for many days, tell a parent or doctor. They can help you feel better.
fact: Constipated means unable to empty your bowels easily.
fact: When you are constipated, your poo is hard, dry, or does not come for days.
fact: Fibre from fruit, vegetables and wholegrain food can help stop constipation.
fact: Drinking plenty of water and moving about also help your bowels work well.
fact: You can say «feel constipated» or «get constipated», and if it lasts a long time, tell a grown-up.
exercise: «After the long journey, Sam felt constipated and had a sore tummy.» What does constipated mean here? | *Unable to empty your bowels easily | Covered in spots | Very thirsty | Feeling sleepy after lunch
exercise: Which foods can help stop you getting constipated? | Fizzy drinks only | Chocolate cake | Crisps and sweets | *Apples, beans and wholegrain bread
exercise: Which of these helps prevent constipation? | Skipping every meal | Eating only sweets | Staying in bed all day with no drinks | *Drinking plenty of water
test: Ravi says, «I feel constipated.» What is he telling us? | *He has a sore tummy and cannot empty his bowels easily | He has a cold and a runny nose | He has won a race | He is very hungry after football
test: Ravi's sore tummy lasts for many days. What is the sensible thing to do? | *Tell a parent or doctor | Stop drinking water | Eat only sweets until it stops | Keep it secret and say nothing
exam: Which sentence uses constipated correctly? | Her new bike was constipated and fast. | The football match was constipated. | The sky was constipated with clouds. | *After three days without a proper poo, Ben felt constipated and had a sore tummy.
